<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 346,200 metric tons (MT) were four and one-fifth times the previous week's marketing-year low and 30 percent above the 4-week average.</p>
<p>The major buyers were Japan (80,900 MT), Taiwan (72,000 MT), Turkey (48,300 MT), the Philippines (39,200 MT), Georgia (25,800 MT), and South Korea (25,700 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 358,600 MT were 37 percent below the week earlier and one-quarter under the 4-week average. The primary destinations were Egypt (52,500 MT), Pakistan (44,700 MT), Israel (36,300 MT), Mexico (33,700 MT), the Philippines (30,500 MT), and Georgia (25,800 MT).</p>
</text>
